%% PL3 p.11: HTTP GET forwarding - the flight is stored on instance 2 only, the client asks instance 1
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Client
    participant I1 as instance1
    participant DB1 as flightops-db-1
    participant I2 as instance2
    participant DB2 as flightops-db-2

    C->>I1: GET /api/scheduled-flights/F<br/>user JWT, X-Request-Id: abc
    I1->>DB1: find F
    DB1-->>I1: not here
    Note over I1: ask the peers one by one<br/>(first peer rotates per request)
    I1->>I2: GET /internal/flights/F<br/>SERVICE JWT, X-Request-Id: abc
    I2->>DB2: find F (local only, never forwards again)
    DB2-->>I2: F
    I2-->>I1: 200 F
    I1-->>C: 200 F<br/>X-Data-Source: peer:instance2
    Note over I1,I2: both logs show [abc]: one request traced across instances
